    "start_line": 30,
    "end_line": 45,
    "lines": [
      "The current Kaggle dataset is mounted at:",
      "",
      "```text",
      "/kaggle/input/datasets/sangiyaparara/tbiom-dataset",
      "```",
      "",
      "The ROF images are under:",
      "",
      "```text",
      "/kaggle/input/datasets/sangiyaparara/tbiom-dataset/data/data/ROF",
      "```",
      "",
      "The research package is under:",
      "",
      "```text",
      "/kaggle/input/datasets/sangiyaparara/tbiom-dataset/rof_tbiom_plan (2)/rof_tbiom_plan"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "manus/data_plan/FINAL_FULL_GUIDE.md",
    "sha256": "2dc910f090d47b521f1fc31365d3bef7dda2aba2909ca4c7fd2dafb66a7203d7",
    "start_line": 73,
    "end_line": 103,
    "lines": [
      "Use the [official ROF repository](https://github.com/ekremerakin/RealWorldOccludedFaces). The repository describes neutral, sunglasses, and masked images and provides `download.py` for obtaining JPG images from the provided pickle files [2].",
      "",
      "Use ROF for:",
      "",
      "- training;",
      "- validation;",
      "- identity-disjoint in-domain testing;",
      "- neutral-to-masked evaluation;",
      "- neutral-to-sunglasses evaluation.",
      "",
      "Do not assume that your downloaded counts will exactly match the counts in the paper or repository. Report the actual local counts.",
      "",
      "### 5.2 MFR2: small external test",
      "",
      "Use the [official MFR2 page](https://sites.google.com/view/masktheface/mfr2-dataset). It reports 53 identities and 269 aligned images, containing masked and unmasked faces. It provides `mfr2_labels.txt` and an official `pairs.txt` containing 848 positive and negative pairs [3].",
      "",
      "Use MFR2 as:",
      "",
      "- an external masked-face verification test;",
      "- a no-fine-tuning transfer benchmark;",
      "- a predefined-pair evaluation.",
      "",
      "Do not use MFR2 as the main training set. It is small and internet-collected.",
      "",
      "### 5.3 RMFRD: larger external test",
      "",
      "Use the [official RMFRD repository](https://github.com/X-zhangyang/Real-World-Masked-Face-Dataset). The repository provides access instructions for real and simulated masked-face datasets [4].",
      "",
      "Use RMFRD as an external test set only after checking:",
      "",
      "- the exact downloaded subset;"
    ]
  },
